title: Case Manager › Page › Links in and the tab address
route: /manager, /manager?tab=cases, /manager?tab=reviews, /active
intro: Nine routes lead to Case Manager. Four of them name a tab in the address. Anything that is not '?tab=reviews' opens Active cases. This diagram lists each source, the address it uses and which tab opens.
dir: LR
also: Links never carry a case, a filter or a page number. Case Manager always opens at the top with filters cleared.
---
start s1 "A person is somewhere else in the demo"

group gOther "Links from other pages"
  click c1 "Eligibility & Benefits › a result › 'Open in Case Manager'\n(shown when the result has no request of its own)"
  process r1 "Go to /manager?tab=cases"
  click c2 "Denial Intelligence › a closed denial › 'Plan the step-down'"
  process r2 "Go to /manager?tab=reviews"
  click c3 "Notifications › 'Denial closed'"
  process r3 "Go to /manager?tab=reviews"
  click c4 "Notifications › 'Drafts updated' (after a payer change)"
  process r4 "Go to /manager (no tab)"
  click c5 "Authorizations queue empty › 'Open Case Manager'\n('Nothing needs you today')"
  process r5 "Go to /manager (no tab)"
  click c6 "New case › 'Case Manager' link above the title,\nor 'Back to Case Manager' on a sent case"
  process r6 "Go to /manager (no tab)"
endgroup

group gShell "Links from the shell"
  click c7 "Sidebar › 'Case Manager'"
  process r7 "Go to /manager (no tab)"
  click c8 "Demo menu › '7 Case Manager: reviews this week'"
  process r8 "Go to /manager?tab=reviews"
  click c9 "A saved or typed old address /active"
  process r9 "Replaced by /manager (any ?tab= on it is lost)"
endgroup

decision d1 "Does the address say ?tab=reviews?"
screen sR "Reviews this week tab opens\nSwitch shows 'Reviews this week' selected"
screen sA "Active cases tab opens\nThe values '?tab=cases', no tab, or anything else all land here"
process p1 "Page starts at the top\nSidebar 'Case Manager' is green\nSearch box empty, all dropdowns on their first option"
click c10 "Click the other tab"
process p2 "Address is rewritten to ?tab=reviews or ?tab=cases in place (no extra Back step)"
goto g1 "Continues in: Case Manager › Reviews this week › The list"
goto g2 "Continues in: Case Manager › Active cases › Being prepared card"
end e1 "Case Manager is open on the right tab"

s1 --> c1 & c2 & c3 & c4 & c5 & c6 & c7 & c8 & c9
c1 --> r1
c2 --> r2
c3 --> r3
c4 --> r4
c5 --> r5
c6 --> r6
c7 --> r7
c8 --> r8
c9 --> r9
r1 & r2 & r3 & r4 & r5 & r6 & r7 & r8 & r9 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| sR --> p1
d1 -->|No| sA --> p1
p1 --> e1
sR --> g1
sA --> g2
sR --> c10 --> p2
sA --> c10
